stsh:SelectQueryTextShape sh:property _:dbba3a9fa74acf0dd0aefa99ad5e9e82 .
_:dbba3a9fa74acf0dd0aefa99ad5e9e82 sh:message "The text of sh:select must be a SELECT query (optional PREFIX and BASE lines, then SELECT)."@en ;
	sh:flags "is" ;
	sh:pattern "^\\s*((PREFIX\\s+[^\\s:]*:\\s*<[^>]*>|BASE\\s+<[^>]*>)\\s*)*SELECT\\b" ;
	sh:path sh:select .
stsh:SelectQueryTextShape sh:targetSubjectsOf sh:select ;
	rdfs:comment "SPARQL Extensions 3: the value of sh:select is a SELECT query. The text must be one: optional PREFIX and BASE lines, then SELECT. An empty string, or text that begins with anything else, is rejected here; the engine otherwise fails with a parse error only when the shapes are run (pySHACL parses it when the shape is loaded). SHACL cannot check the rest of the grammar, so a query that begins correctly but is malformed is still the engine's to report. Applies wherever sh:select is used: a SPARQL constraint, a SELECT validator, a SPARQL target, a node expression written in place."@en ;
	rdfs:label "Text of a sh:select is a SELECT query"@en ;
	a sh:NodeShape .
